    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YUwbTNFP92MbconEgCJZPM)_\n\n**Before:** in many modules the options of a package sat in top-level `setq` forms just before or after its `use-package`.\n\n**After:** in 14 modules those options are `:custom` entries of the package's `use-package`, in the `.org` docs (canonical) and in the tangled `.el`. Attached comments and trailing comments moved with their setting. The doc text says where each option now lives (bullets, no leftover sections for removed code blocks).\n\n| Module | Package | Moved |\n|---|---|---|\n| sp-denote | denote | `denote-directory`, `denote-save-buffers` |\n| sp-consult-snapfile | consult-snapfile | 3 options |\n| sp-citations | citar | `citar-library-file-extensions` |\n| sp-litnotes | citar-denote | 4 options |\n| sp-bibprocess | bibtex | 6 `bibtex-autokey-*` |\n| sp-org-node-mem | org-node | 2 options |\n| sp-org-refile | org-refile | 3 options |\n| sp-vulpea-ext | vulpea-capf | 3 options |\n| sp-vulpea-ui | vulpea-ui | 13 options |\n| sp-dired | dirvish | `dirvish-preview-buffers-max-count` |\n| sp-graphs | discourse-graphs | 10 `dg-*` options |\n| sp-org-agenda | org-agenda | 14 `org-agenda-*` options |\n| sp-org-base | org | 3 options |\n| sp-fonts | lin | `lin-face`, `lin-mode-hooks` |\n\n**Behaviour that changes (check these):**\n- `:custom` uses `customize-set-variable`, so a variable with a `:set` function now runs it; `setq` did not. I did not read the installed packages' source to see which have one.\n- `:custom` runs before `:init` and `:config`. For `discourse-graphs` the `dg-*` options used to be set after `discourse-graphs-mode` was turned on; `citar-denote` and `org-node` likewise enable their mode after the options now.\n- `sp-org-refile`, `sp-consult-snapfile` and `sp-vulpea-ui` have `:after`, so their options now apply once that package has loaded, not at module load.\n- `sp-org-agenda` sets `org-agenda-tags-column` twice (0, then `org-tags-column`), as before; the last one wins.\n- `sp-citations`: the existing `:custom` already holds a `(when …)` and a `(setq citar-notes-paths …)` form, which `use-package` reads as variables named `when` and `setq` (the doc already says so). The new entry was added after them and is a normal one.\n\n**Not tested:** no Emacs here, so nothing was loaded or byte-compiled. What I did run: a Python check that every changed `.el` has the same bracket balance as before, and a Python tangler that shows each doc tangles to its `.el` (the same 15 pre-existing mismatches, such as `sp-icons` and `sp-themes`, before and after). `python3 tools/set-defcustom-group.py --check` fails on `main` too, for `sp-collection-query-tables{,-org,-views}.el`; I did not touch those.\n\n**Conflicts:** rebased onto `main` with #85 (merged), clean. #79 also adds a line under \"Open pull requests\" in `CHANGELOG.org`, next to mine; keep both lines. No other open PR touches these files.\n\n**Not moved** (built-in features, settings of a package declared elsewhere, order-sensitive ones, unloaded modules) is listed in the thread.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01PF79fi4scSSid1V5FvNkEF)_",
